cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "anySQL: SQL analytics for AI systems"
abstract: >-
  anySQL is an open-source Python library for querying LLM responses, agent
  traces and RAG pipelines with standard SQL. Wrappers for OpenAI and
  Anthropic clients, an agent tracer and a RAG tracer normalise telemetry into
  six canonical PyArrow tables, which are held in memory, optionally persisted
  to SQLite, and queried through DuckDB. Built-in queries cover multi-model
  comparison, prompt regression detection, cost attribution, agent debugging,
  and RAG forensics, where a shared query id joins retrieved chunks to eval
  results to separate retrieval failures from generation failures.
authors:
